    },
    {
      "id": "1557335673269256195",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-07T10:15:58.405+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "## Dicing Metal\nWe do not want to dice through features or test patterns. Apparently it loads up the wheel and that causes heat/ time from wheel dressing and other bad things. \n\nFirst one, they requested we ask GF to not let test features cross our dicing lines. \nSecond one (and I don't even know how/if this is even possible?? but they asked if there was a way for GF to not have metal deposited in the un-shot spaces",
      "author": {
        "id": "756011607603019777",
        "name": "anfroholic",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Andrew Wingate",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [
          {
            "id": "1423020172595298314",
            "name": "Mod",
            "color": null,
            "position": 4
          }
        ],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-10_media/67bd670a335a2f955fb2ded57088a2cb-675B3.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
      "embeds": [],
      "stickers": [],
      "reactions": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "inlineEmojis": []
    },
    {
      "id": "1557335708006481941",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-07T10:16:06.687+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": "2026-10-07T10:16:42.33+00:00",
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "In the pic posted with < 50um dimension, AFAICT that's just the polyimide deposition. but you can cut through that, doesn't matter for anything, there is nothing there. The 60.90 is the actual point where things start to matter ( that's the `Metal5` from the guard ring which extends all the way to the edge of the project dies )",
      "author": {
