    {
      "id": "1557338000034238514",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-07T10:25:13.149+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "## Dicing plan\nThey really don't need a whole lot it turns out. \nWe need to give them the centerlines of every cut. They load those in and it just patterns after that. \nBasically said the table like we have and a picture of the reticle helps. \n\n### Main takeaway\nWe need to call out the part that is the test pattern and the little sliver if it exists *as if they were dies* and they should be a part of the table too.",
      "author": {
        "id": "756011607603019777",
        "name": "anfroholic",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Andrew Wingate",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [
          {
            "id": "1423020172595298314",
            "name": "Mod",
            "color": null,
            "position": 4
